  "bibliography": {
    "abstract": "This research examines the critical risks associated with implementing Performance-Based Contracting (PBC) in Saudi Arabia’s road maintenance sector, a key component of Vision 2030's infrastructure objectives. Despite PBC’s global success in improving service delivery and cost efficiency, its adoption in Saudi Arabia faces operational, managerial, and contextual challenges. An expert survey of 93 professionals from government, contracting, and consulting organizations identified 23 risk factors, with the top 10 including weak contractor performance, unexpected traffic growth, skill gaps, infrastructure deterioration, and early contract termination, further validated using Structural Equation Modelling (SEM). SEM confirmed significant relationships and met reliability and validity criteria, highlighting contractor and planning-related risks. Spearman's rank correlation and risk allocation analyses revealed differing stakeholder perceptions and informed balanced risk-sharing strategies. The findings provide actionable guidance for contractor vetting, capacity building, traffic management, and institutional oversight, offering a data-driven framework to optimize PBC performance in Saudi road maintenance.",
